                                        "entry_id": "f6934824-5f20-329c-a6b2-f754de004e91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In civil proceedings, the party responding to the complaint; one who is sued and called upon to make satisfaction for a wrong complained of by another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd21ebd4-9425-44f0-8fd5-8fc46dfff28c",
                                                "sense_id": "1e168027-5965-3234-84a1-73e91f601dac",
                                                "text": "404(b)—including a series of domestic abuse incidents defendant perpetrated against victim, a PFA against defendant by victim, and other third-party PFAs entered against defendant to protect other women—as well as evidence from[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a33028b3-5f1e-30a8-a380-079d221c92ab",
                                        "entry_id": "f6934824-5f20-329c-a6b2-f754de004e91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In criminal proceedings, the accused."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69a75736-7dca-442e-b315-1c36ed7b03bf",
                                                "sense_id": "a33028b3-5f1e-30a8-a380-079d221c92ab",
                                                "text": "Unintended mathwashing occurs when the algorithm is left unchecked, and, learning from historical data, amplifies social bias. The U.S. justice system uses an algorithm called COMPAS to determine a criminal's likelihood to re-offend. COMPAS has been proven by Pro Publica to predict that black defendants will have higher rates of recidivism than they actually do, while white defendants are predicted to have lower rates than they actually do."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
